tatement below?\n\nThe ratio of parrots to ducks is $6:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there are $6$ parrots for every $\\boxed{}\\,$ ducks." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074391 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0691c732-4d32-5281-9884-b582edd2db81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074391 #edb/ref 1074 "Since there are $18$ parrots and $15$ ducks, the ratio of parrots to ducks is $18:15.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,18 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,15 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,6 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThat means that $6:5$ is equivalent to $18:15.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of parrots to ducks is $6:5\\,$ because there are $6$ parrots for every $5\\,$ ducks.\"\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074634 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074634 #edb/ref 1061 186681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074634 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6aa20fa4-3163-5025-84f7-a1ddd4324cd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074634 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186075034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074635 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074635 #edb/ref 1061 186682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074635 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4854b84c-59a0-5a98-a9c6-9b8427de8ab8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074635 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186075035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074636 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074636 #edb/ref 1061 186683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074636 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "55be2711-44d0-588a-899f-562ac0853236" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074636 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074637 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074637 #edb/ref 1061 186686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074637 #edb